 "notes": "95% CL upper limit on g_phigamma from Keck Array 2012-2015 search for axion-induced CMB polarization oscillations. Curve is the paper's smoothed analytic approximation Eq. 15, provided explicitly 'for convenient replotting': g < 4.3e-12 GeV^-1 * sinc^-1(m/5.0e-19 eV) * (m/1e-21 eV) * (kappa*rho0/0.3 GeV/cm^3)^-1/2 * [1 - 2(m/m0)^-2 (1-cos(m/m0))]^-1/2, m0=1.9e-23 eV, evaluated with kappa*rho0 = 0.3 GeV/cm^3 (kappa=1, i.e. axions are all of the local DM). Mass range = analysis range: m_min=1.2e-23 eV to m_max=2*pi*0.5/hr=5.7e-19 eV. Validated against the vector Fig. 3 (exclusion.pdf in e-print): matches the cyan 'Keck 2012-2015 smoothed' curve to ~1%; the jagged blue observed limit fluctuates about it (median ratio ~0.95, local spikes up to ~2x and larger near the longest periods/avoidance frequencies). Paper notes these limits do not exclude new regions relative to existing astrophysical bounds, but they are the paper's own direct measured exclusion.",
